        "subject": "LU-15909 lnet: use 64-bit selection sequence numbers",
        "message": "LU-15909 lnet: use 64-bit selection sequence numbers\n\nLNet breaks ties between nets, NIs and peer NIs by round robin. Each\nselection copies a send counter into the chosen object. The object\nwith the lowest value wins the next tie.\n\nThe counters are 32 bits. After a wrap the newest object holds the\nlowest value. It then wins every tie until the counter again passes\nthe values that the other objects kept. Round robin stops for a full\nwrap period.\n\nMake ln_net_seq, lp_send_seq, net_seq, ni_seq, lpn_seq and lpni_seq\nu64. They then do not wrap in practice.\n\nFixes: 05413b3d84f7 (\"LU-15713 lnet: Ensure round robin across nets\")\nFixes: a18c4a16246e (\"LU-13575 lnet: Ensure round robin selection of local NIs\")\nFixes: c51763948abf (\"LU-13575 lnet: Ensure round robin selection of peer NIs\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: I442cb9d0328c4f85429607899461700725b70467\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
